as we see in #4644.  however, the nesting is still there for now and going back to many versions, it doesn't actually make sense.   the Transaction object does not point to the previous Transaction object, and the management of the \"reset agent\" which we unfortunately still need for some two-phase types of situations is all over the place.\r\n\r\nbasic demo of nesting not even making sense:\r\n```\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\n\r\n\r\npg_url = \"postgresql://scott:tiger@localhost/test\"\r\n\r\nengine = create_engine(pg_url, echo=True, echo_pool='debug')\r\n\r\nconn = engine.connect()\r\n\r\n\r\nt1 = conn.begin()\r\n\r\nt2 = conn.begin()\r\n\r\nt3 = conn.begin()\r\n\r\nassert t3._parent is t1  # shouldn't this be t2?\r\nassert t2._parent is t1\r\n\r\nt3.rollback()\r\n\r\n\r\nassert not t3.is_active\r\nassert not t1.is_active\r\n\r\nassert not t2.is_active   # fails - t2 was just forgotten\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\nsee if we can revise the nesting model and localize how reset agent gets set up, then again it may not be worth it as 2.0 has a simpler model.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.co